cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "MOB-ERA-GEE for Multivariate Longitudinal Outcomes"

message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this software repository and the
  associated article listed under preferred-citation.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Sunmee
    affiliation: "University of Manitoba"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3723-9974"

repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantMM/MOB-ERA-GEE-Longitudinal-public"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Research software implementing a fixed-component longitudinal specialization
  of ERA-GEE combined with model-based recursive partitioning (MOB) for detecting
  subgroup heterogeneity in multivariate longitudinal intercept and slope
  parameters. The repository includes seeded synthetic-data examples,
  implementation checks, and simulation-based validation under the reference
  design used for the accompanying empirical study. No Canadian Longitudinal
  Study on Aging (CLSA) data are required or redistributed.

keywords:
  - model-based recursive partitioning
  - MOB
  - generalized estimating equations
  - GEE
  - extended redundancy analysis
  - ERA-GEE
  - longitudinal data
  - multivariate outcomes
  - parameter instability
  - subgroup heterogeneity

